(283319, 19963, 7743, '<td valign="top">Good composition and contrast.<br/> <br/>Depth of field is a little shallow or the focus is not sharp.  The landscape mode on the camera or setting the aperture to the smallest possible (largest number) would help for this type of image.  If focus is the issue then using a faster shutter speed or a tripod and the self timer/remote would help keep the image in sharp focus.  Even the pushing of the shutter button can move the camera enough to put an image out of focus.</td>', 'Good composition and contrast. Depth of field is a little shallow or the focus is not sharp.  The landscape mode on the camera or setting the aperture to the smallest possible (largest number) would help for this type of image.  If focus is the issue then using a faster shutter speed or a tripod and the self timer/remote would help keep the image in sharp focus.  Even the pushing of the shutter button can move the camera enough to put an image out of focus.', '2003-04-30 12:23:32.000000', NULL, 1),
