(283362, 19887, 7743, '<td valign="top">I''m guessing that evaluative metering was used here which makes the foreground and part of the trains very dark.  There are two ways that would bring the train out more.<br/> <br/>1.  Take a reading (evaluative) with less sky in the picture, lock the exposure and recompose - all done with the shutter button pressed half way.  Then push the shutter button the rest of the way.<br/> <br/>2. (Easier) Use spot metering on the area of the picture you want to expose for, recompose and take the picture.</td>', 'I''m guessing that evaluative metering was used here which makes the foreground and part of the trains very dark.  There are two ways that would bring the train out more. 1.  Take a reading (evaluative) with less sky in the picture, lock the exposure and recompose - all done with the shutter button pressed half way.  Then push the shutter button the rest of the way. 2. (Easier) Use spot metering on the area of the picture you want to expose for, recompose and take the picture.', '2003-04-30 12:39:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(283364, 19910, 6870, '<td valign="top">Really nice idea. The idea could perhahps be better communicated with a more interesting or dramatic point of view.</td>', 'Really nice idea. The idea could perhahps be better communicated with a more interesting or dramatic point of view.', '2003-04-30 12:39:24.000000', NULL, 1),
