(289187, 20035, 7358, '<td valign="top">phat</td>', 'phat', '2003-05-06 13:20:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(289205, 19897, 7711, '<td valign="top">Good focus on the subject, but I would have chosen a shallower DOF to throw those distracting background items out of focus. I like that you played on the brown tones in the rusted old wheels when colouring this picture, but I can''t say I agree with how you choose to compose this shot. I thought about whether I wanted a tighter crop or a wider angle, and come to the conclusion that neither would have improved this one for me. Perhaps if you shot just the round wheels in behind sitting on the rails without the big one in front, it would have been a more interesting shot? These are just a few ideas -- feel free to disregard some or all! :)</td>', 'Good focus on the subject, but I would have chosen a shallower DOF to throw those distracting background items out of focus. I like that you played on the brown tones in the rusted old wheels when colouring this picture, but I can''t say I agree with how you choose to compose this shot. I thought about whether I wanted a tighter crop or a wider angle, and come to the conclusion that neither would have improved this one for me. Perhaps if you shot just the round wheels in behind sitting on the rails without the big one in front, it would have been a more interesting shot? These are just a few ideas -- feel free to disregard some or all! :)', '2003-05-06 13:34:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(289208, 20039, 7711, '<td valign="top">Hmm...what sort of car is this? its a shiney engine, so maybe if you either shot closer or even wider we''d have a bit of context, but I suspect you were going for the abstract feel of an engine, in which case, zoom on in and go a bit to your left to get a better view on those cool engine parts, rather than cutting off the corners of it. :)</td>', 'Hmm...what sort of car is this? its a shiney engine, so maybe if you either shot closer or even wider we''d have a bit of context, but I suspect you were going for the abstract feel of an engine, in which case, zoom on in and go a bit to your left to get a better view on those cool engine parts, rather than cutting off the corners of it. :)', '2003-05-06 13:37:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(289229, 19753, 7711, '<td valign="top">What a bird''s eye view! You''ve included too much background in this shot, (IMO) and the little boat gets lost as our eyes are draw to the mountains and the line where the water meets the shore. A tighter crop that placed your subject somewhere that conformed with the rule of thirds might have yielded a more effective photograph for you! :) (just my two cents, I claim no special knowledge!)</td>', 'What a bird''s eye view! You''ve included too much background in this shot, (IMO) and the little boat gets lost as our eyes are draw to the mountains and the line where the water meets the shore. A tighter crop that placed your subject somewhere that conformed with the rule of thirds might have yielded a more effective photograph for you! :) (just my two cents, I claim no special knowledge!)', '2003-05-06 13:47:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(289232, 19591, 7711, '<td valign="top">fabulous action shot, I love the motion blur, I feel dizzy just looking at the background. :) Wish more of the lasso and horse''s tail were in the shot, but those are nitpicks! I am curious how many voters will have said "this isn''t transportation, its a rodeo!" A horse is a horse (though).. of course... (sorry, couldn''t resist!)</td>', 'fabulous action shot, I love the motion blur, I feel dizzy just looking at the background. :) Wish more of the lasso and horse''s tail were in the shot, but those are nitpicks! I am curious how many voters will have said "this isn''t transportation, its a rodeo!" A horse is a horse (though).. of course... (sorry, couldn''t resist!)', '2003-05-06 13:50:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(289234, 20018, 7711, '<td valign="top">Shadows are harsh, and this has the feel of more of a snapshot than a picture whose composition was carefully thought out -- I say this because of the harsh light and blown out highlights on the bike helmet combined with the shadows on the face. Cute puppy thought! :)</td>', 'Shadows are harsh, and this has the feel of more of a snapshot than a picture whose composition was carefully thought out -- I say this because of the harsh light and blown out highlights on the bike helmet combined with the shadows on the face. Cute puppy thought! :)', '2003-05-06 13:56:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(289237, 19637, 8286, '<td valign="top">Nice.  I like the angle and depth of field.  But a little over saturated.</td>', 'Nice.  I like the angle and depth of field.  But a little over saturated.', '2003-05-06 13:58:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(289239, 20036, 8286, '<td valign="top">The depth of field here is excellent.  I think the blacks could be a tiny bit richer.</td>', 'The depth of field here is excellent.  I think the blacks could be a tiny bit richer.', '2003-05-06 14:01:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(289249, 19621, 7711, '<td valign="top">I love the idea you had here, the negative space is very artistic, but I would have balanced it out so the wheel made up one quarter of the whole shot. The biggest problem here is that the wheel is very pixely and out of focus, which makes me think you probably had to do a lot of cropping and interpolating to get this shot up to the size you wanted for submission. There is a great tutorial on the site on how to sample up that might help in that regard! :)</td>', 'I love the idea you had here, the negative space is very artistic, but I would have balanced it out so the wheel made up one quarter of the whole shot. The biggest problem here is that the wheel is very pixely and out of focus, which makes me think you probably had to do a lot of cropping and interpolating to get this shot up to the size you wanted for submission. There is a great tutorial on the site on how to sample up that might help in that regard! :)', '2003-05-06 14:24:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(289252, 20022, 7711, '<td valign="top">great subject! :) I would have preferred to see more of the car in the shot, as well, the lighting (which must be its display lighting or that in combination with your flash) is making the shot look a bit flat, but I''m afraid I don''t have any practical suggestions on how to improve that. <br/>As a pure asthetic preference: would it have been possible to get a sideview of the car instead?</td>', 'great subject! :) I would have preferred to see more of the car in the shot, as well, the lighting (which must be its display lighting or that in combination with your flash) is making the shot look a bit flat, but I''m afraid I don''t have any practical suggestions on how to improve that. As a pure asthetic preference: would it have been possible to get a sideview of the car instead?', '2003-05-06 14:34:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(289254, 19586, 7711, '<td valign="top">This is rather morbid (which can be effective in its "shock" value),but I''m afraid this doesn''t meet the challenge, and is additionally  a bit dark and out of focus with washed out colours. Try using software to saturate the colours and play with the brightness and contrast perhaps? :)</td>', 'This is rather morbid (which can be effective in its "shock" value),but I''m afraid this doesn''t meet the challenge, and is additionally  a bit dark and out of focus with washed out colours. Try using software to saturate the colours and play with the brightness and contrast perhaps? :)', '2003-05-06 14:37:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(289256, 19821, 7870, '<td valign="top">Very effective!</td>', 'Very effective!', '2003-05-06 14:41:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(289261, 19756, 7711, '<td valign="top">As I am sure I among the last commentators, I won''t belabour that i think this shot is too far from the subject and its very grainy without any artistic reason I can think of, and its out of focus. That said, I do like the capture of the rainbow and think you had a great idea here! :)</td>', 'As I am sure I among the last commentators, I won''t belabour that i think this shot is too far from the subject and its very grainy without any artistic reason I can think of, and its out of focus. That said, I do like the capture of the rainbow and think you had a great idea here! :)', '2003-05-06 14:43:39.000000', NULL, 1),
