(289807, 19621, 3607, '<td valign="top">i didn''t vote on this image, and having read through the comments, yeah the quality/pixelation etc (i don''t know if that was intentional or not, but if it is, in the future you might want to add that to your comment box above, although we can only see it after the fact ;-).<br/> <br/>all that said, there is no way this photo should have come in last place.  this photo shows excellent contrast of object and the nothing-ness white background, its obviously a wheel, one of the keys the the rise of human civilization and transportation, and its got a cool edgy look.  keep on shoot''n.  tom<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-05-07 00:19:18.</i></td>', 'i didn''t vote on this image, and having read through the comments, yeah the quality/pixelation etc (i don''t know if that was intentional or not, but if it is, in the future you might want to add that to your comment box above, although we can only see it after the fact ;-). all that said, there is no way this photo should have come in last place.  this photo shows excellent contrast of object and the nothing-ness white background, its obviously a wheel, one of the keys the the rise of human civilization and transportation, and its got a cool edgy look.  keep on shoot''n.  tom', '2003-05-07 01:18:38.000000', '2003-05-07 01:19:18.000000', 0),
(289808, 19991, 327, '<td valign="top">Congrats Mag. wonderful.<br/></td>', 'Congrats Mag. wonderful.', '2003-05-07 01:19:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(289809, 19991, 326, '<td valign="top">Great use of leading lines.....Well done &amp; Congrats!</td>', 'Great use of leading lines.....Well done & Congrats!', '2003-05-07 01:19:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(289810, 19808, 811, '<td valign="top">At least we can count it as a learning experience. <br/>I find it interesting that it does seem that you are the focus of the picture, when in reality that was not even realized until you saw it on the lcd!  <br/>I agree about the crop, and that it needs to have the symbol and you more off-center, and you could correct that if we had the ability to crop.  Until then, try to compose carefully in the viewfinder!<br/>I''m not sure about the oversharpened comment, as no sharpening was done to it, but the dirt may give that impression somewhat.  Antialiasing is when a rounded edge looks square, basically.  There''s not a lot we can do with that, given our current circumstances.  Maybe someday when you are rich and famous and can use something other than school material!!  Hey, look on the bright side, <b>you</b> can always blame your  photography teacher! :-)  I on the other hand, have no excuse!</td>', 'At least we can count it as a learning experience. I find it interesting that it does seem that you are the focus of the picture, when in reality that was not even realized until you saw it on the lcd!  I agree about the crop, and that it needs to have the symbol and you more off-center, and you could correct that if we had the ability to crop.  Until then, try to compose carefully in the viewfinder!I''m not sure about the oversharpened comment, as no sharpening was done to it, but the dirt may give that impression somewhat.  Antialiasing is when a rounded edge looks square, basically.  There''s not a lot we can do with that, given our current circumstances.  Maybe someday when you are rich and famous and can use something other than school material!!  Hey, look on the bright side, you can always blame your  photography teacher! :-)  I on the other hand, have no excuse!', '2003-05-07 01:19:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(289811, 19969, 5925, '<td valign="top">I knew this picture was top material!  Congratulations!</td>', 'I knew this picture was top material!  Congratulations!', '2003-05-07 01:19:42.000000', NULL, 0),
