(291458, 19381, 7775, '<td valign="top">the object in the background is my computer chair.  the idea was that most of my "travelling" is done virtually.  on the web i''ve been around the world in back.  using my own two feet i haven''t really ventured outside of my own province.  originally i took the photo with the shoes in focus. but the point was the shoes aren''t used much.  that''s why they are sitting on the floor abandon and lonely.  so i took a few with them out of focus and then mussied the picture up a little.  it kind of give me that long lost memory feeling.  thanks for all the feedback though.</td>', 'the object in the background is my computer chair.  the idea was that most of my "travelling" is done virtually.  on the web i''ve been around the world in back.  using my own two feet i haven''t really ventured outside of my own province.  originally i took the photo with the shoes in focus. but the point was the shoes aren''t used much.  that''s why they are sitting on the floor abandon and lonely.  so i took a few with them out of focus and then mussied the picture up a little.  it kind of give me that long lost memory feeling.  thanks for all the feedback though.', '2003-05-07 22:06:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(291463, 19718, 509, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everyone for their comments and votes.  With the top of the skate in focus, it really wasn''t as interesting, hence the shallow dof used.  I would''ve liked it even shallower, but without macro lenses I think that''s the best my camera can do in that respect.  I think I should have tried harder to hide the hockey stick so the skate wouldn''t be cropped so tightly on top, but I''m surprised noone mentioned that.<br/> <br/>I''ve posted a pic of the setup <a href="//www.pbase.com/image/16415461" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">here</a>  ---I''ve taken the picture down to free up space---<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-05-30 23:40:35.</i></td>', 'Thanks to everyone for their comments and votes.  With the top of the skate in focus, it really wasn''t as interesting, hence the shallow dof used.  I would''ve liked it even shallower, but without macro lenses I think that''s the best my camera can do in that respect.  I think I should have tried harder to hide the hockey stick so the skate wouldn''t be cropped so tightly on top, but I''m surprised noone mentioned that. I''ve posted a pic of the setup here  ---I''ve taken the picture down to free up space---', '2003-05-07 22:14:37.000000', '2003-05-31 00:40:35.000000', 0),
(291555, 19991, 2989, '<td valign="top">Just awesome work here!  And another ribbon in your profile, just like that.  Congratulations!  Reading some of the comments were actually insipiring - I wish I could call this mine.  We have no underground transportation in the city at all.  Looks like a great place to take shots.  Keep up the good work!</td>', 'Just awesome work here!  And another ribbon in your profile, just like that.  Congratulations!  Reading some of the comments were actually insipiring - I wish I could call this mine.  We have no underground transportation in the city at all.  Looks like a great place to take shots.  Keep up the good work!', '2003-05-07 23:31:31.000000', NULL, 0),
